# Unary minus at the int64 boundary.
#
#   r1  n = INT64_MIN   `-n == n` holds (the wrap) and `n < 0` holds, so both
#                       rules fire; `n < 0` rules out 0, where `-0 == 0` too.
#   r2  n = -1          the control: `-(-1)` is 1, so only `boundary` fires,
#                       which a negation that did nothing could not produce.
assert Big entity_id=r1 n=-9223372036854775808
pump
assert Big entity_id=r2 n=-1
pump
